  "body": "## The bug that was eating configuration\n\nSaving anything in the admin Configuration page rewrote `~/.fcc/.env` from the manifest, so **every key the manifest did not know about was silently deleted**:\n\n```\nkey                            kept   written back\nMODEL                          yes    yes\nREQUEST_LOG_MAX_ROWS           NO     NO\nFALLBACK_FIRST_TOKEN_TIMEOUT   yes    NO\nLOG_LEVEL                      yes    NO\n```\n\nA raised `REQUEST_LOG_MAX_ROWS` reverted to the default on the next unrelated save — which is why a retention cap that had been raised to 500k kept behaving like 50k.\n\nSaving now writes back any key `Settings` still reads, under its own heading. A key that configures nothing is still dropped, so a retired provider option retires rather than being preserved forever (this keeps the existing stale-key behaviour that `test_admin_apply_omits_stale_zai_base_url` covers).\n\n## Promoted from module constants to settings\n\nTuning these previously meant editing installed source:\n\n| Setting | Was | What it costs |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `PROVIDER_RETRY_ATTEMPTS` | `UPSTREAM_TRANSIENT_TOTAL_ATTEMPTS=5` | ~30s of backoff before a healthy fallback is tried |\n| `STREAM_MIDSTREAM_RECOVERY_ATTEMPTS` | `=5` | bounds how long a dying stream holds a request |\n| `STREAM_COMMIT_HOLDBACK_SECONDS` | `EARLY_HOLDBACK_SECONDS=0.75` | width of the invisible-recovery window |\n| `STREAM_EARLY_RETRY_ATTEMPTS` | `EARLY_TRANSPARENT_TOTAL_ATTEMPTS=5` | retries before routing sees a failure |\n| `RATE_LIMIT_COOLDOWN_SECONDS` | `=60` | pause when a 429 carries no `Retry-After` |\n| `CREDENTIAL_CIRCUIT_THRESHOLD` | `=3` | failures before one key is benched |\n| `REQUEST_LOG_TEXT_MAX_CHARS` | `MAX_TEXT_CHARS=50000` | also bounds what content search can find |\n| `REQUEST_LOG_COMPRESSION_LEVEL` | `=9` | level 19 measured 4.9% smaller at 1/9 the speed |\n| `REQUEST_LOG_QUEUE_MAX_SIZE` | `=10000` | pending writes before records are dropped |\n\nA holdback of `0` now commits the first event immediately rather than buffering it until some later push happens to check the clock.\n\n## New \"Limits\" section\n\n18 fields: the four fallback deadlines, the nine above, and request-log retention/capture/compression. Each carries a description saying what the value costs, not just what it is.\n\nA test asserts **every field's default equals the code's own default** — a form that shows a different number than the server uses is a lie, and that class of drift is exactly what made the retention cap confusing.\n\n## Verification\n\nFailure sets compared against untouched `main`, by test ID: **50 before, 50 after, zero new**. (An earlier version of that comparison was broken — it stripped test names and compared 50 identical `FAILED` strings — so the numbers here are from the corrected one.)\n\nThe websearch-log fields were dropped from this change: they already exist in the `websearch` section, generated from the catalog, and my first pass duplicated them. The new tests caught it.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
